etencies to care for every resident in a way that maximizes each resident's well being.","category":"Nursing and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0760":{"code":"F-0760","title":"Ensure that residents are free from significant medication errors.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0607":{"code":"F-0607","title":"Develop and implement policies and procedures to prevent abuse, neglect, and theft.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0609":{"code":"F-0609","title":"Timely report suspected abuse, neglect, or theft and report the results of the investigation to proper authorities.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0610":{"code":"F-0610","title":"Respond appropriately to all alleged violations.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0732":{"code":"F-0732","title":"Post nurse staffing information every day.","category":"Nursing and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0812":{"code":"F-0812","title":"Procure food from sources approved or considered satisfactory and store, prepare, distribute and serve food in accordance with professional standards.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0880":{"code":"F-0880","title":"Provide and implement an infection prevention and control program.","category":"Infection Control Deficiencies","concept":"infection_prevention","concept_label":"Infection prevention"},"cms-f0700":{"code":"F-0700","title":"Try different approaches before using a bed rail.  If a bed rail is needed, the facility must (1) assess a resident for safety risk; (2) review these risks and benefits with the resident/representative; (3) get informed consent; and (4) Correctly install and maintain the bed rail.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0578":{"code":"F-0578","title":"Honor the resident's right to request, refuse, and/or discontinue treatment, to participate in or refuse to participate in experimental research, and to formulate an advance directive.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0641":{"code":"F-0641","title":"Ensure each resident receives an accurate assessment.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0645":{"code":"F-0645","title":"PASARR screening for Mental disorders or Intellectual Disabilities","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0656":{"code":"F-0656","title":"Develop and implement a complete care plan that meets all the resident's needs, with timetables and actions that can be measured.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0690":{"code":"F-0690","title":"Provide appropriate care for residents who are continent or incontinent of bowel/bladder, appropriate catheter care,  and appropriate care  to prevent urinary tract infections.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0756":{"code":"F-0756","title":"Ensure a licensed pharmacist perform a monthly drug regimen review, including the medical chart, following irregularity reporting guidelines in d